---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <p class="cmd"><span class="you">andrew@pope</span> ~ <span class="sigil">$</span> whoami</p>

  <h1>Andrew Pope<span class="cursor"></span></h1>
  <p class="muted">
    Air Force officer. I build at the edge of hardware and AI, and write down
    what I actually learn doing it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Right now I'm teaching myself how modern chips work from the physics up —
    logic gates to CPUs to AI accelerators — and building a tinywhoop flight
    controller around an STM32G473 to keep it honest. Alongside that:
    on-device inference and agentic tooling. I'm early in most of this. I'd
    rather show the work than claim I've arrived.
  </p>

  <p class="cmd">
    <span class="you">andrew@pope</span> ~ <span class="sigil">$</span> cat now.txt
  </p>
  <ul class="entry-list">
    <li>
      <span class="entry-title">Circuit Box</span>
      <span class="badge">building</span>
      <p class="entry-desc">
        An interactive logic-circuit builder that climbs the full ladder of
        abstraction — one gate up to a working 8-bit CPU.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="entry-title">Chip course</span>
      <p class="entry-desc">
        How computers are built, from physics up — anchored to real hardware,
        not slides.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="cmd">
    <span class="you">andrew@pope</span> ~ <span class="sigil">$</span> cat why.txt
  </p>
  <p>
    I think we've gotten comfortable being unambitious, and a quiet nihilism is
    filling the gap. I'm Christian — I don't believe we engineer our way out of
    every problem we create. But my honest read is simpler than that: if we
    stay here, we die. So I point my work at the physical bottlenecks between us
    and a future worth wanting — trusted silicon, on-device intelligence, and
    eventually getting off this planet.
  </p>

  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:2rem;">
    <a href="/work">work</a> · <a href="/writing">writing</a> ·
    <a href="/apps">apps</a>
  </p>
</Base>
